meta {
  name: Get analysis run by id
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/children/{{childId}}/analysis-runs/{{runId}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # GET /api/children/{childId}/analysis-runs/{runId}

  One run's full detail, including its sections — used by the child-level Analysis tab when a
  specific run is selected (`?run=`). Note `childId` in the route is not re-checked against the run
  (`GetRunAsync` looks the run up by `runId` alone and authorizes against the run's *own*
  `childProfileId`); a mismatched `childId` in the URL still returns the run as long as the caller
  has access to the child the run actually belongs to.

  ## Responses

  - `200` — `data: AnalysisRunDto`, with `sections` populated (ordered by `displayOrder`):
    - Ordinary sections (`sectionKind` e.g. `present_levels`, `services`, `evaluation_results`, …,
      a short snake_case label chosen by the model) populate `analysis` (an
      `AnalysisRunSectionResult`: `plainLanguageSummary`, `keyPoints[]`, `redFlags[]`,
      `legalReferences[]`); `goalAnalyses`/`etrCompleteness`/`etrEligibility` are `null`.
    - `sectionKind: "iep_goals"` (IEP sources only, one per IEP source with any ratings) instead
      populates `goalAnalyses[]` and leaves `analysis` `null`. Every `goalAnalyses[].goalId` is
      validated against the source IEP's current goals server-side before being persisted.
    - `sectionKind: "etr_completeness"` / `"etr_eligibility"` (ETR sources only, at most one of each
      per ETR source) instead populate `etrCompleteness` / `etrEligibility` respectively; either may
      be absent if the model omitted it, which is not a source failure.
    - A section whose stored JSON fails to deserialize maps to all of `analysis`/`goalAnalyses`/
      `etrCompleteness`/`etrEligibility` being `null` rather than throwing.
  - `sources[]` — one per selected document: `status` (`Pending | Running | Completed | Error`) and
    `errorMessage` track that source's own Claude call independently of the run's overall `status` —
    one source can be `Error` while the run as a whole is `Completed` with the rest.
  - `401` — missing/invalid bearer token.
  - `404` — run not found, or the caller has no access to the child the run belongs to.

